; Regression (2026-11-08): an inner name after a TUPLE type -- `(int, bool).X`
; -- names nothing: only a record has inner records. The grammar reads inner
; names after any type's arguments (scaly.sgm InnerType), and the Modeler
; writes this one as a type no record can be, so the planner reports it where
; it is written instead of dropping the name (Modeler.handle_tuple_inner#).
; xfail: unknown type
let x: (int, bool).X 5
print "`x`"
